WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:03.567
-Far-right congresswoman
Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:04.567
joked over the weekend
that if she

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:06.334
and former Trump adviser
Steve Bannon

00:00:06.334 --> 00:00:09.534
had been in charge of the
insurrection on January 6th,

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:11.701
they would have been armed
and they would have won.

00:00:11.701 --> 00:00:13.434
The comments come
as Greene prepares

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:15.033
to take on an influential role

00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:17.634
in the new GOP majority
in the House.

00:00:17.634 --> 00:00:19.501
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:19.501 --> 00:00:22.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.834 --> 00:00:25.434
As we've been discussing
for the past few weeks,

00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:28.000
the GOP performance
in November's midterm elections

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.133
was one of the worst outcomes
for an opposition party

00:00:30.133 --> 00:00:32.033
in the last 100 years
of American politics.

00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:34.734
For example, not a single
Democratic incumbent

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:36.200
in the Senate lost re-election,

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:39.968
despite running in battleground
states like Georgia, Nevada,

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:41.501
New Hampshire, and Arizona.

00:00:41.501 --> 00:00:42.567
In fact...

00:00:50.234 --> 00:00:52.100
That's right, the last time
Republicans did this badly

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:53.634
was the Great Depression,

00:00:53.634 --> 00:00:55.868
and a great depression is where
Donald Trump now finds himself.

00:00:55.868 --> 00:00:58.868
The dude -- The dude
is a recluse now.

00:00:58.868 --> 00:01:00.601
He doesn't go anywhere.

00:01:00.601 --> 00:01:03.367
Spends all his time moping
around his Palm Beach hotel

00:01:03.367 --> 00:01:05.901
like a ghost from
a Stephen King novel

00:01:05.901 --> 00:01:08.734
where the ghost's too lazy
to scare anyone.

00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:10.133
[ As Trump ] Here's Donald.

00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:12.400
And also, boo.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.133
Boo, as they say. Boo.

00:01:14.133 --> 00:01:16.234
Did I scare you?
Did you hear me?

00:01:16.234 --> 00:01:18.501
Did you hear me
lumbering down the hallway

00:01:18.501 --> 00:01:22.634
with loose change jangling in
the pockets of my giant coat?

00:01:22.634 --> 00:01:24.100
You're not scared at all?

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:28.968
Well, that's too bad, because
my head is stuck in this door.

00:01:28.968 --> 00:01:30.901
So if you wouldn't mind,
could you butter up my neck

00:01:30.901 --> 00:01:33.267
so I can slip out
and be on my way?

00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:34.534
Also, redrum.

00:01:34.534 --> 00:01:36.868
We love redrum, don't we, folks?

00:01:36.868 --> 00:01:38.634
People say
it's "murder" backwards.

00:01:38.634 --> 00:01:40.834
I don't see it.

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:42.367
[ Normal voice ]
The GOP performance was so bad

00:01:42.367 --> 00:01:45.601
that even Donald Trump,
a man who craves the spotlight

00:01:45.601 --> 00:01:47.467
more than he craves food
and water --

00:01:47.467 --> 00:01:48.767
or I guess food and Diet Coke --

00:01:48.767 --> 00:01:51.634
has essentially been forced
into isolation,

00:01:51.634 --> 00:01:53.000
as "The Washington Post"
reported...

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:05.567
And you know what?
Fine.

00:02:05.567 --> 00:02:08.067
He's a 76-year-old former
business idiot from Queens.

00:02:08.067 --> 00:02:10.501
That's what he should be doing,
playing golf in Florida

00:02:10.501 --> 00:02:12.601
and watching "Yellowstone"
on an 80-inch TV

00:02:12.601 --> 00:02:14.534
with his remotes Velcroed
to the coffee table.

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:17.634
This is what
keeps him preoccupied.

00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:19.701
Just shuttling him
back and forth

00:02:19.701 --> 00:02:21.667
between his golf course
and Mar-a-Lago,

00:02:21.667 --> 00:02:23.033
that's a win for everyone.

00:02:23.033 --> 00:02:24.434
Hell, let's use taxpayer dollars

00:02:24.434 --> 00:02:27.133
to build a high-speed rail line
that only he can use,

00:02:27.133 --> 00:02:29.901
or if a high-speed rail
is too expensive,

00:02:29.901 --> 00:02:31.801
we can just put cannons
on each side of the lake

00:02:31.801 --> 00:02:33.834
to launch him back and forth.

00:02:33.834 --> 00:02:36.667
Also, I want to emphasize again,
Trump's isolation started

00:02:36.667 --> 00:02:39.968
after he announced he was
running for president again.

00:02:39.968 --> 00:02:42.501
It's one thing to say,
"I just lost my re-election bid.

00:02:42.501 --> 00:02:44.367
I'm going to take some time
to myself,"

00:02:44.367 --> 00:02:45.901
and then go into seclusion.

00:02:45.901 --> 00:02:48.834
But it's crazy to do it
after announcing

00:02:48.834 --> 00:02:51.467
you're running for the most
powerful office in the world.

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:52.901
Probably just lies
in bed all day

00:02:52.901 --> 00:02:54.601
with noise-canceling
headphones on

00:02:54.601 --> 00:02:56.133
listening to his old speeches.

00:02:56.133 --> 00:02:57.934
-I know windmills very much.

00:02:57.934 --> 00:02:59.267
They're noisy.

00:02:59.267 --> 00:03:00.968
They kill the birds.

00:03:00.968 --> 00:03:03.200
You want to see
a bird graveyard?

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.801
Go under a windmill someday.

00:03:05.801 --> 00:03:07.434
-Melania standing at the door

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:09.067
trying to get him
to come out for dinner.

00:03:09.067 --> 00:03:10.334
"Donald, you have to eat.

00:03:10.334 --> 00:03:11.868
You have to eat, Donald.

00:03:11.868 --> 00:03:13.934
When I try and slide
the hamburger under the door,

00:03:13.934 --> 00:03:17.701
the top of the bun comes off.

00:03:17.701 --> 00:03:21.167
It's getting ketchup
all over the door, Donald."

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:23.534
So now Republicans are trying
to figure out what happened.

00:03:23.534 --> 00:03:24.767
Some are playing the blame game

00:03:24.767 --> 00:03:26.100
and pointing fingers
at each other.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:28.601
For example, conservatives
have been saying they lost

00:03:28.601 --> 00:03:31.000
because they don't use
mail balloting like Democrats,

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.234
although they can't quite
seem to figure out

00:03:33.234 --> 00:03:34.567
whose fault that is.

00:03:34.567 --> 00:03:37.467
-We need to not just
compete for votes, for ballots.

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:38.934
We need to compete for ballots.

00:03:38.934 --> 00:03:41.000
If we don't bank ballots early,
we're going to keep losing.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.000
-We didn't.
-But we didn't.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.467
-But we didn't do it in 2020

00:03:44.467 --> 00:03:46.434
'cause everyone said don't vote
early 'cause that's corrupt.

00:03:46.434 --> 00:03:49.267
-Not everyone.
-Well, a lot of people did

00:03:49.267 --> 00:03:51.133
at the very top
of the Republican Party.

00:03:51.133 --> 00:03:54.501
-I think Republicans have been
unwilling, for whatever reason,

00:03:54.501 --> 00:03:59.467
reluctant, resistant to voting
early and voting by mail.

00:03:59.467 --> 00:04:01.734
-Is it really a mystery
to you guys?

00:04:01.734 --> 00:04:03.634
These two would make
such terrible detectives

00:04:03.634 --> 00:04:05.067
on "Law &amp; Order."

00:04:05.067 --> 00:04:08.067
"Weird, this guy's just lying on
the floor for whatever reason.

00:04:08.067 --> 00:04:09.667
Excuse me, sir.
Who murdered you?

00:04:09.667 --> 00:04:10.834
He's not going to talk.

00:04:10.834 --> 00:04:13.601
This is going to be
a tough nut to crack."

00:04:13.601 --> 00:04:15.234
But now that more data
is coming in

00:04:15.234 --> 00:04:16.701
about who voted in the midterms,

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:19.267
it turns out Republicans didn't
actually have a turnout problem.

00:04:19.267 --> 00:04:20.434
They had a candidate problem.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.634
Even Republican voters
couldn't bring themselves

00:04:43.634 --> 00:04:45.567
to vote for Republican
candidates, and you know why?

00:04:45.567 --> 00:04:47.934
They all tried to be Trump,
but only Trump can be Trump.

00:04:47.934 --> 00:04:50.000
Yes, Trump is
a monstrous sociopath,

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:53.267
but he was able to conceal
that reality from some voters

00:04:53.267 --> 00:04:55.167
by also being a sweaty,
bumbling oaf

00:04:55.167 --> 00:04:57.467
who would ramble about
sexy New York yacht parties

00:04:57.467 --> 00:04:59.467
in the '80s to an audience
of Boy Scouts

00:04:59.467 --> 00:05:02.601
or dance to the Village People
when he went onstage

00:05:02.601 --> 00:05:05.501
and complain nonstop at rallies
about how low water pressure

00:05:05.501 --> 00:05:07.234
was causing America's toilets
not to flush.

00:05:07.234 --> 00:05:10.200
That same shtick doesn't work
for other Republicans

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:13.100
or other Democrats or literally
any other human being alive.

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:15.467
Like remember
Herschel Walker's weird rant

00:05:15.467 --> 00:05:18.267
about vampires and werewolves
that turned off so many voters?

00:05:18.267 --> 00:05:19.968
-The other night,
I was watching this movie.

00:05:19.968 --> 00:05:22.434
I was watching this movie called
"Fright Night," "Freak Night,"

00:05:22.434 --> 00:05:24.868
some type of night,
but it was about vampires.

00:05:24.868 --> 00:05:26.000
I don't know if you know,

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.601
vampires some cool people,
are they not?

00:05:27.601 --> 00:05:29.567
But I'm going to tell you
something that I found out.

00:05:29.567 --> 00:05:31.968
A werewolf can kill a vampire.
Did you know that?

00:05:31.968 --> 00:05:34.200
I never knew that, so I didn't
want to be a vampire anymore.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.601
I wanted to be a werewolf.

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:40.400
-When Walker said that, everyone
was like, "What the [bleep]"

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:43.200
But if you imagine Trump
doing the same bit,

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:45.334
you can almost see it working.

00:05:45.334 --> 00:05:47.501
[ As Trump ] The other night
I was watching "Freak Night"

00:05:47.501 --> 00:05:49.167
or "Fright Night"
or some kind of night.

00:05:49.167 --> 00:05:51.367
We all love the freaks and
the frights, don't we, folks?

00:05:51.367 --> 00:05:54.300
And it was about vampires,
and I said to myself,

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:57.133
"Vampires are some cool people,
are they not?"

00:05:57.133 --> 00:05:59.234
It's so true, and you're
hearing it more and more.

00:05:59.234 --> 00:06:01.734
Some of my best friends
are vampires, except...

00:06:05.167 --> 00:06:07.200
...except the one I know
loves garlic.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:08.501
It's funny.
It's the opposite.

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:11.534
But then I found out
werewolves can kill vampires.

00:06:11.534 --> 00:06:13.033
The fake news,
they won't tell you that.

00:06:13.033 --> 00:06:14.534
They want you to think vampires

00:06:14.534 --> 00:06:17.901
are more powerful than
werewolves, but it's a hoax.

00:06:20.367 --> 00:06:22.167
Because the sun comes out
every day,

00:06:22.167 --> 00:06:24.133
but it's very tricky
to find a silver bullet,

00:06:24.133 --> 00:06:26.100
because every bullet
looks silver,

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:28.000
but then you shoot the werewolf
and it keeps coming.

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:30.133
You say, "Uh-oh.

00:06:30.133 --> 00:06:32.100
I don't think that bullet
was silver."

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:33.467
It's very unfair.

00:06:33.467 --> 00:06:35.467
It's very unfair
when you get the bullet

00:06:35.467 --> 00:06:38.200
that looks silver
but isn't silver.

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:41.067
Very unfair
how they're treating me.

00:06:41.067 --> 00:06:43.067
How they're treating me with
the bullets that look silver

00:06:43.067 --> 00:06:44.934
that aren't silver.

00:06:44.934 --> 00:06:48.534
Of course, my favorite werewolf
is my son Don Jr.

00:06:48.534 --> 00:06:50.834
[ Laughter ]

00:06:50.834 --> 00:06:52.200
[ Normal voice ] Republicans
thought they could keep

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:54.033
just doing Trump's routine,

00:06:54.033 --> 00:06:55.734
but even their own voters
rejected it,

00:06:55.734 --> 00:06:58.133
resulting in yet another
repudiation at the ballot box

00:06:58.133 --> 00:07:00.934
and a historic performance
by Democrats.

00:07:00.934 --> 00:07:03.367
And yet some of the GOP's
most prominent politicians

00:07:03.367 --> 00:07:06.367
are still leaning further in
the direction of MAGA extremism

00:07:06.367 --> 00:07:07.667
after it was rejected by voters.

00:07:07.667 --> 00:07:09.267
Georgia congresswoman
Marjorie Taylor Greene,

00:07:09.267 --> 00:07:12.467
for example, appeared at
a Republican gala in Manhattan

00:07:12.467 --> 00:07:13.968
over the weekend
and apparently decided

00:07:13.968 --> 00:07:16.234
that one of the biggest issues
facing Americans right now

00:07:16.234 --> 00:07:18.501
is the availability of sex toys
at department stores.

00:07:35.734 --> 00:07:38.300
Yeah, no one wants to hear
about butt plugs and dildos

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:40.167
during dessert,
especially on a night

00:07:40.167 --> 00:07:41.901
when the dessert
is banana split.

00:07:41.901 --> 00:07:43.334
[ Laughter ]

00:07:43.334 --> 00:07:45.300
Also, even if they do
sell those items,

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:46.934
I can't imagine
they're easy to get.

00:07:46.934 --> 00:07:49.667
I mean, you can't even
pick up toothpaste at CVS

00:07:49.667 --> 00:07:50.968
without pushing a little button

00:07:50.968 --> 00:07:53.234
and waiting for
the world's sleepiest person

00:07:53.234 --> 00:07:55.200
